# Customers API: VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP Client / Visual Studio .http
# Start the stack first (Aspire AppHost or `dotnet run --project src/OrderManagement.Api`).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5050

### 1. Get a development token (mock Entra; Development only)
# @name token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Steve", "roles": ["Orders.Write"] }

###
@accessToken = {{token.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Create a customer (201 + Location)
# @name createCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Lerato Mokoena", "email": "lerato.mokoena@example.co.ls", "countryCode": "LS" }

###
@customerId = {{createCustomer.response.body.id}}

### 3. Get it back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Search (name or email prefix), paged and sorted (the brief's unversioned route works too)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers?search=ler&page=1&pageSize=20&sort=-createdAt
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5. Validation errors: 400 with one message per field
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "email": "not-an-email", "countryCode": "KE" }

### 6. Duplicate email (case-insensitive): 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Someone Else", "email": "LERATO.MOKOENA@example.co.ls", "countryCode": "ZA" }

### 7. Page size above 100: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers?pageSize=500
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
